# Omarchy kids mode: the apps a child install starts with denied, one desktop
# id per line, copied into /etc/omarchy/parent/apps.deny the first time the
# app list is applied; edit that file afterwards, not this one. Peter's policy
# for an eleven-year-old (plans/kids-apps-themes.md): the supervision tier,
# which a parent opens with `sudo omarchy-kids apps allow NAME` when needed,
# and the hidden tier of terminals, developer tools, and disks. An id that is
# not installed matches nothing and does no harm.

# Only with supervision
localsend
localsend_app
com.moonlight_stream.Moonlight
com.obsproject.Studio

# Terminals and developer tools. The terminal itself stays on Super+Return for
# the parent (foot is on the never-close list); only its launcher entries hide.
foot
foot-server
footclient
btop
nvim

# Disks and administrative tools
org.gnome.DiskUtility
avahi-discover
bssh
bvnc
